This task implements PRD-G in full. It decomposes into six tightly coupled sub-systems that must land together for a coherent feature.

1. **State machine module** (`rust/limux-host-linux/src/agent_state.rs` or `limux-core` if socket fields live there):
   - Define an enum `AgentState { Unknown, Running, NeedsInput, Idle }` and a struct `SurfaceAgentState { state: AgentState, kind: Option<AgentKind>, last_event_at: Instant, acknowledged: bool }`.
   - Implement `transition(current, event) -> AgentState` following the state model table:
     - agent started / prompt submitted / tool activity → `Running`
     - awaiting user input / permission request / needs attention → `NeedsInput`
     - stop / end-of-turn → `Idle`
     - no hook data → `Unknown` (never guessed)
   - Per-surface aggregation to workspace: any NeedsInput → NeedsInput; else any Running → Running; else any Idle → Idle; else Unknown.
   - Record `AgentKind` per surface (feeds agents-status family column; precedent `AgentHookSessionRecord`, agent_hooks.rs:85).
   - Eviction on surface/pane/tab close (Codex-required — closed surface stuck in needs-input would pin aggregate forever; eviction test required).
   - Operator interaction does NOT mutate state; visual urgency uses a separate `acknowledged` bit that clears on focus, mirroring unread. Socket-reported state and sidebar never disagree.
   - Stale-state decay: `Running` with no hook events for a configurable period degrades to `Unknown`. Default 30 min. Must be testable with an injected clock (no sleeps in tests).
   - Unit-testable without GTK; GTK wiring separate (docs/maintainability.md).
   - Persistence: runtime-only, NOT persisted to session.json. Restored workspaces start Unknown.

2. **Hook path extension** (`rust/limux-cli/src/main.rs`):
   - Add a new control method `surface.agent_event` — additive, classified in PRD-E registry as mutation (plain additive fields if PRD-G ships first).
   - The shim makes `surface.agent_event` a SECOND fire-and-forget call AFTER the existing awaited `notification.create` (main.rs:1125-1131). Connect+write timeout 2 s, failures silent — hook latency budget stays within the existing 5 s hook-side budget.
   - Hook shims stamp events with surface identity exactly as today (`LIMUX_SURFACE_ID` env contract) — no new env vars required.
   - Event authenticity: any socket peer can emit surface.agent_event (same trust model as notification.create today — LocalUser mode). Note in registry's restricted-surface review that surface.agent_event should NOT be in the Cursor-restricted allowlist.

   Pseudo-code for hook shim addition:
   ```rust
   // After existing notification.create call completes or fails:
   fn emit_agent_event(surface_id: &str, event: AgentEvent, agent_kind: Option<AgentKind>) {
       let msg = ControlMessage::new("surface.agent_event")
           .arg("surface_id", surface_id)
           .arg("event", event)
           .arg("agent_kind", agent_kind)
           .build();
       match connect_timeout(SOCKET_PATH, Duration::from_secs(2)) {
           Ok(mut stream) => { let _ = stream.write_all(msg.as_bytes()); }
           Err(_) => {} // silent failure
       }
   }
   ```

3. **Per-family installer mapping fixes** (delivered via `limux hooks setup` re-run; no manual user config edits):
   - **hermes**: no change — reference family. Events: pre_llm_call / pre_approval_request / post_llm_call (main.rs:1170-1187). Reachable: ALL.
   - **claude**: remap installer from `("Notification", "stop")` to `("Notification", "notification")` (main.rs:1709, parse_hook_event main.rs:1012-1017). Today the positional event WINS over JSON hook_event_name, causing needs-input to arrive as stop = INVERTED to idle. Side effect / bug fix: "Claude finished" toast on Notifications becomes "Claude needs you".
   - **codex**: SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit/Stop only today (main.rs:1693-1701) — no needs-input source. Wire the Codex notification-class event if its hook vocabulary offers one; else document needs-input as unreachable for codex v1 in the checklist doc.
   - **gemini**: SessionStart/BeforeAgent/AfterAgent/SessionEnd today (main.rs:1714-1723) — same treatment as codex. Wire notification-class event if available; else document unreachable.
   - **opencode**: plugin maps session.idle/updated/status/compacted → prompt-submit, NO stop-class event (main.rs:2210-2213) → idle unreachable, idle agents look running. Rework plugin mapping: `session.idle` → stop-class.
   - **Tool-activity keepalive**: no family installs tool-activity hooks today (only parser recognizes them, main.rs:1183-1185). Wire PreToolUse/PostToolUse-class events for families that support them (claude does) as the `running` keepalive. For families without, decay default is 30 min and mid-turn decay behavior is documented.

4. **Sidebar rendering** (`window.rs` sidebar row builder):
   - Render a compact state indicator (icon or colored glyph + accessible tooltip naming the state) for the aggregated workspace state on sidebar rows.
   - `needs-input` is visually dominant AND distinct from unread dot AND distinct from PRD-D attention border. The distinctness matrix axes: {needs-input indicator on|off} × {unread dot on|off} × {attention border on|off} = 8 combinations. Xvfb suite asserts widget/CSS-class presence structurally for all 8; PLUS one rendering assertion each for running, idle, and unknown indicator variants.
   - State transitions arrive without focus changes (background workspace row updates when agent stops — Xvfb fake-agent test).
   - Preserve the existing targeted per-row widget update pattern (retained gtk::ListBoxRow + label/CSS mutations, window.rs:3506-3521/4810/6390). This is a REGRESSION GUARD-RAIL — the sidebar already does targeted updates; do NOT rebuild list models per update.
   - Instrumentation counter behind `debug.*` (precedent `debug.flash.count`): increments on row RE-CREATION and on full sidebar_list repopulation — those are the named increment sites. A test pushing 100 state updates across 20 workspaces asserts counter == 0.
   - Batching: bursts of hook events within one frame coalesce to one row update (existing GTK idle/tick pattern; test with 50-event burst).
   - Aggregation lives with the state machine module, not scattered in UI code.

5. **Socket exposure** (additive fields, no renames):
   - `workspace.list` responses gain additive `agent_state` field (aggregated workspace state).
   - `pane.surfaces` responses gain additive `agent_state` field (per-surface state).
   - Per PRD-E registry conventions if landed; plain additive fields if PRD-G ships first.
   - New CLI convenience `limux agents-status [--json]`: one table — workspace, pane/surface, agent family (from hook metadata when known), state, age of last event. Optionally fold in `surface.health` if trivially available from the same call path; else defer (open question 2 default: yes if trivial).

6. **Documentation**:
   - Per-family reachable-state matrix documented in the checklist doc — unreachable states per family are documented, never silently wrong.
   - docs/maintainability.md: note GTK wiring is separate from pure state machine module.
   - PR description includes wall-time numbers for 100-update scenario (target: no worse than 2× single-update cost).

   Pseudo-code for state machine:
   ```rust
   pub enum AgentState { Unknown, Running, NeedsInput, Idle }
   pub enum AgentEvent { Started, PromptSubmitted, ToolActivity, NeedsInput, Stop }
   pub struct SurfaceAgentState {
       state: AgentState,
       kind: Option<AgentKind>,
       last_event_at: Instant,
       acknowledged: bool,
   }
   fn transition(current: AgentState, event: AgentEvent) -> AgentState {
       match event {
           AgentEvent::Started | AgentEvent::PromptSubmitted | AgentEvent::ToolActivity => AgentState::Running,
           AgentEvent::NeedsInput => AgentState::NeedsInput,
           AgentEvent::Stop => AgentState::Idle,
       }
   }
   fn aggregate_workspace(surfaces: &[(SurfaceId, &SurfaceAgentState)]) -> AgentState {
       if surfaces.iter().any(|(_, s)| s.state == NeedsInput) { NeedsInput }
       else if surfaces.iter().any(|(_, s)| s.state == Running) { Running }
       else if surfaces.iter().any(|(_, s)| s.state == Idle) { Idle }
       else { Unknown }
   }
   fn check_decay(state: &mut SurfaceAgentState, now: Instant, decay: Duration) {
       if state.state == Running && now.duration_since(state.last_event_at) > decay {
           state.state = Unknown;
       }
   }
   ```

   Pseudo-code for sidebar targeted update (regression guard):
